From 3f7b0c1a4e6d4a2f8c9b5d1e2a3f4c5b6d7e8f90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Lundby <Eric.Lundby@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:10:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Use gfortran-style LAPACK symbol names for OpenBLAS (win-arm64)

When configure cannot find a Fortran compiler, CoinUtils falls back to a
hard-coded name mangling. That is the case for this Windows recipe, since it
only requires compiler('fortran') on unix. The fallback defaults to MKL-style
(uppercase) names.

win-64 links mkl_rt.lib, which exports DGETRF/DGETRS, so uppercase is correct
there. win-arm64 links OpenBLAS, which exports the gfortran-style dgetrf_ and
dgetrs_, so DGETRF/DGETRS stay unresolved and every downstream executable
fails to link (e.g. clp: unresolved external symbol DGETRS).

Select the else branch, which defines the gfortran-style names.

Why not just add a Fortran compiler to the build requirements instead? That is
not a fix, for two reasons:

  * It only sets F77_FUNC indirectly. configure.ac calls AC_COIN_PROG_F77 and
    defines the mangling only if that probe finds a working compiler, so a
    failed probe silently leaves the uppercase fallback in place - producing a
    package that builds fine and is still unlinkable.
  * It has a real cost. flang carries a *strong* run_export
    ("libflang >=20.1.8"), and strong run_exports from build-only deps are
    applied to the output. coin-or-utils would gain an unused libflang runtime
    dependency, and so would everything that links it (clp, cbc, osi, ...).

Selecting the branch here is deterministic and costs nothing.

Note this header is only compiled into CoinUtils itself (the block is guarded
by defined(COINUTILS_BUILD)) and the installed header is the generated
config_coinutils.h, so downstream consumers are unaffected.
---
 CoinUtils/src/CoinUtilsConfig.h | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CoinUtils/src/CoinUtilsConfig.h b/CoinUtils/src/CoinUtilsConfig.h
index e5f1a2b..9d3c4d7 100644
--- a/CoinUtils/src/CoinUtilsConfig.h
+++ b/CoinUtils/src/CoinUtilsConfig.h
@@ -50,7 +50,12 @@
 #if defined(COINUTILS_BUILD) && !defined(F77_FUNC)
-#if 1
+/* OpenBLAS exports gfortran-style names (dgetrf_); MKL exports uppercase
+   (DGETRF). Use the gfortran convention when linking OpenBLAS.
+   Adding a Fortran compiler build dependency is not a fix: it only defines
+   F77_FUNC indirectly via configure's probe (which can silently fail), and
+   flang's strong run_export would force an unused libflang runtime dep. */
+#if 0
 # define F77_FUNC(name,NAME) NAME
 # define F77_FUNC_(name,NAME) NAME
 #else
 # define F77_FUNC(name,NAME) name ## _
 # define F77_FUNC_(name,NAME) name ## __
-- 
2.30.1

